1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:12,690
You can save any table as a spreadsheet file.

2
00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:16,550
Here are your closed trades for the last month.

3
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,760
Click Export CSV.

4
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,620
It tells you what will be saved: the table, and how many rows and columns.

5
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,980
Click Export and the file opens in your spreadsheet app, such as Excel.

6
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:33,790
Or Cancel if you change your mind.

7
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:37,300
Export CSV works the same on every table in the app.

